.TH FIND 1
.SH NAME
find \- files with an attribute
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B find
.IB key = value
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B find
is a command built into the shell,
.BR sh (1).
It prints the path of every file whose attribute
.I key
is
.I value
(set with
.BR tag (1)),
anywhere on the disk, one per line. It reads only the attribute index, not
the directories.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0, or 1 on failure.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
find project=SIEOS
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tag (1),
.BR siefs (5)
.SH BUGS
Not Unix's
.BR find :
it does not walk directories or match names. Only values of at most 255
bytes are indexed.
